wayland.xml is wayland 1.23, taken from wayflan's own vendored copy.  It is
here for gate 8 and for nothing else: wayflan generates the core protocol into
its own package, so nothing under src/protocol/ compiles this file.

Vendoring it is what makes gate 8 total rather than partial.  The gate checks
that every event we listen for exists on the interface we listen for it on, by
reading the XML in this directory — so an interface whose XML is absent is a
handler the gate cannot see.  We listen to wl_output for its name and its scale
factor, because river_output_v1 carries neither, and without this file that was
exactly the shape of handler gate 8 was written to catch.
